  "report_period": "Week 29 (10th Jul to 17th Jul 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Nereus Shipping have committed their Capesize \"Heroic\" 182/2010 Odense, Denmark (SS 10/2030, DD 10/2027) at USD 32,8 mill. Remind you that back in February, same owners sold the sister vessel \"Epic\" 182/2010 Odense, Denmark (SS 07/2030, DD 08/2027) at USD 32,2 mill. The Post Panamax \"Indus Prosperity\" 93/2011 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 07/2026) of MSPL was committed to Greek interests at USD 13,5 mill. Note that a week ago, the \"Ocean Rhea\" 92/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS 07/2031, DD 07/2029) was sold at USD 15,25 mill. Ince Shipping have committed their Ultramax \"Ince Beylerbeyi\" 61/2012 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027) to clients of ADNOC at rgn USD 22 mill. By way of comparison, the \"ASL Ixora\" 61/2012 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027) was sold in April at same levels. On the Supramax sector, Hai Phuong committed the \"HPC Atlantic\" 56/2013 Minaminippon, Japan (SS 10/2030, DD 10/2028) at USD 19,5 mill, while the \"Ocean Bright\" 56/2013 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 08/2028) was sold in June at USD 19,5 mill also. Moreover, Thoresen Shipping committed their \"Thor Infinity\" 52/2002 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS/DD 01/2027) to Chinese interests at USD 7,8 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Grace Bali\" 52/2002 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 09/2030, DD 08/2028) was sold in June at USD 8,8 mill. The Handysize \"Blue Union Alpha\" 28/2011 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 09/2026) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 9,65 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Beetle\" 28/2012 Imabari, Japan (SS 04/2030, DD 2/2028) was sold a month ago at USD 12,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "Tsakos Shipping & Trading have committed their Suezmax \"Alaska\" & \"Archangel\" 163/2006 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD passed & SS 01/2031, DD 01/2029, Ice Class 1A) at xs USD 50 mill each. Note that the one-year- younger \"Cosmo Sail\" 159/2007 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 07/2027) was sold a month ago at USD 49,5 mill. Minerva Marine have committed their MR2 \"Minerva Rita\" 50/2005 Stx, Korea (SS 10/2030, DD 09/2028, Ice Class 1A) at USD 16,2 mill. For reference, the two-years-younger \"Gemini Pearl\" 50/2007 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 05/2027) was sold back in May at USD 17 mill. Moreover, the \"MFM Memphis\" 48/2011 Iwagi, Japan (SS 09/2030, DD 07/2028) was sold at high USD 26 mill, while the smaller \"UOG Kyma\" 45/2011 Onomichi, Japan (SS/DD 07/2026) was sold in April at USD 25,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates West Australia/China fluctuated, with Dampier and Port Hedland to Qingdao settling between USD 12.45/13.50 fio. In the Atlantic, Tubarao to Qingdao routes achieved USD 34.85 fio, while runs from Saldanha Bay and Nouadhibou to Qingdao secured USD 23.49 fio and USD 35.75 fio respectively. Transatlantic runs from Narvik to Rotterdam made USD 10.90 fio, and Tubarao to Eren fetched USD 29.85 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "Ιn the Pacific, NoPac rounds or multi-laden legs trips from Japan, North China and South China with Singapore/Japan or worldwide redelivery secured between USD 16,500/20,000 pd. On Australian business, departures via Australia settled between USD 14,900/20,000 pd to Singapore/Japan and USD 14,750/21,000 pd to China/India ranges. Indonesian coal runs from South China and South East Asia via Indonesia saw redelivery to South China between USD 11,500/22,000 pd, with further runs to South Korea, Singapore/Japan, and Japan ranges settling between USD 14,000/19,000 pd. Further activity in the East included trips from South China and South East Asia via ECSA to Singapore/Japan range settling between USD 17,000/22,000 pd. In the Atlantic, Continent departures fixed via US Gulf to Continent at USD 25,000 pd. On period, Kamsarmaxes achieved USD 16,500 pd for 5/7 months and USD 21,000 pd for 6/8 months, while another secured 97% of BPI for 12 months.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, NoPac rounds and local trips from North China with South East Asia and Singapore/Japan redelivery secured USD 16,000/22,000 pd. For longer runs from North China, a trip to the Med reached USD 26,000 pd, a run to West Africa achieved USD 23,000 pd and a trip to the US Gulf fixed at USD 14,500 pd. From South China and South East Asia, coal and nickel ore runs to China and South East Asia fetched USD 15,000/18,000 pd, while a barites trip from South China to the US Gulf achieved USD 15,500 pd. From India, a trip to China fixed at USD 17,500 pd, while PG and India departures to local ranges settled between USD 15,500/22,750 pd. In the Atlantic, US Gulf departures to NCSA and ECSA secured USD 25,000/27,000 pd, a USEC run to East Med made USD 31,500 pd and ECSA trips to NCSA fetched USD 26,000 pd. ECSA backhauls to Continent, India and Singapore/Japan ranges achieved USD 28,000/39,000 pd. From the Black Sea/Med, a Black Sea run to South East Asia settled at USD 28,000 pd and an East Med trip via Black Sea to South Korea made USD 21,000 pd. From South and East Africa, runs to China and Far East ranges obtained USD 18,000/24,000 pd. On period, an Ultramax fixed from South East Asia for 4/6 months duration at USD 22,000 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Atlantic, ECSA departures secured between USD 18,500/27,000 pd for grain trips to NCSA, US Gulf and WCSA ranges. Out of the US Gulf, wood pellets runs settled at USD 22,000 pd to the Continent and USD 23,000 pd to Japan, while a trip to China achieved USD 21,750 pd. From the Continent, a prompt grain run to West Africa achieved USD 14,750 pd."
    }
  },
